      "progress": { "current": 49, "total": 80 },
      "milestone_payload": {
        "title": "MODULE COMPLETED!",
        "badge_emoji": "🔁",
        "completed_topic": "Used to / Would (Past Habits)",
        "xp_earned": 60,
        "milestone_progress": "Module 6/9 Clear",
        "motivational_quote": "Officer level trap crack kar diya! Ab sequence of tense ke sabse bade traps dekhte hain."
      },
      "navigation": { "next": "card_50_before_after", "button_text": "Start Next Module ➔" }
    },

    {
      "card_id": "card_50_before_after",
      "card_slug": "card_50_before_after",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "sequence_of_tense",
      "level": 7,
      "progress": { "current": 50, "total": 80 },
      "messages": [
        { "speaker": "aman", "text": "Ab hum seekhenge special time-clause words jo Past Perfect ko 'trigger' karte hain. Pehla: 'Before' aur 'After'." },
        { "speaker": "raju", "text": "Sir ye 'before/after' to hum pehle bhi use kar chuke the na?" },
        { "speaker": "aman", "text": "Haan par ab pattern fix karte hain: 'Before' clause ke baad Simple Past, aur dusra clause Past Perfect ho sakta hai (jo pehle hua). 'After he had finished dinner, he went to sleep.'" },
        { "speaker": "raju", "text": "Matlab 'After' ke saath Past Perfect (pehle wala kaam), aur baad wale part mein Simple Past?" }
      ],
      "navigation": { "next": "card_51_by_the_time", "button_text": "Next Card ➔" }
    },

    {
      "card_id": "card_51_by_the_time",
      "card_slug": "card_51_by_the_time",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "sequence_of_tense",
      "level": 7,
      "progress": { "current": 51, "total": 80 },
      "messages": [
        { "speaker": "aman", "text": "Sahi Raju! Ab dusra pattern: 'By the time'. Rule: 'By the time' + Simple Past, Main Clause + Past Perfect. 'By the time the police arrived, the thief had escaped.'" },
        { "speaker": "raju", "text": "Toh thief pehle bhaga (had escaped), police baad mein aayi (arrived)?" },
        { "speaker": "aman", "text": "Ekdum sahi logic! 'By the time' clause hamesha 'later' event dikhata hai (Simple Past), aur main clause 'earlier completed' event (Past Perfect)." },
        { "speaker": "raju", "text": "Achhaaaa, matlab 'by the time' khud Simple Past leta hai, dusra part Past Perfect!" }
      ],
      "navigation": { "next": "card_52_no_sooner_than", "button_text": "Next Card ➔" }
    },

    {
      "card_id": "card_52_no_sooner_than",
      "card_slug": "card_52_no_sooner_than",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "sequence_of_tense",
      "level": 7,
      "progress": { "current": 52, "total": 80 },
      "messages": [
        { "speaker": "aman", "text": "⭐ BPSC/SBI PO ka sabse favourite structure: 'No sooner + had + Subject + V3 + than + Simple Past'. 'No sooner had he reached the station than the train left.'" },
        { "speaker": "raju", "text": "Sir isme 'had' subject se pehle kyun hai? Ulta lag raha hai!" },
        { "speaker": "aman", "text": "Bahut acha observation! Jab sentence 'No sooner' se shuru hota hai, to Inversion hota hai — had aur subject ki jagah badal jaati hai. Ye special exam trick hai." },
        { "speaker": "raju", "text": "Aur 'than' ke baad 'the train left' — ye Simple Past hi rahega, 'had left' nahi?" }
      ],
      "navigation": { "next": "card_53_hardly_scarcely", "button_text": "Next Card ➔" }
    },

    {
      "card_id": "card_53_hardly_scarcely",
      "card_slug": "card_53_hardly_scarcely",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "sequence_of_tense",
      "level": 7,
      "progress": { "current": 53, "total": 80 },
      "messages": [
        { "speaker": "aman", "text": "Bilkul sahi! Aur 'No sooner...than' jaisi hi do aur cousin structures hain: 'Hardly had...when' aur 'Scarcely had...when/before'. 'Hardly had I sat down when the phone rang.'" },
        { "speaker": "raju", "text": "Matlab teeno structures same pattern follow karte hain — bas connecting word alag hai?" },
        { "speaker": "aman", "text": "Exactly Raju! 'No sooner' ke saath 'than' aata hai, par 'Hardly/Scarcely' ke saath 'when' ya 'before' aata hai — 'than' NAHI. Ye mixing exam ka sabse bada trap hai!" },
        { "speaker": "raju", "text": "⭐ Note: No sooner-than, Hardly/Scarcely-when/before. Kabhi mix nahi karna!" }
      ],
      "navigation": { "next": "card_54_as_soon_as", "button_text": "Next Card ➔" }
    },

    {
      "card_id": "card_54_as_soon_as",
      "card_slug": "card_54_as_soon_as",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "sequence_of_tense",
      "level": 7,
      "progress": { "current": 54, "total": 80 },
      "messages": [
        { "speaker": "aman", "text": "Last pattern: 'As soon as'. Ismein dono clauses SIMPLE PAST hote hain, Past Perfect ki zaroorat nahi. 'As soon as he saw me, he smiled.'" },
        { "speaker": "raju", "text": "Hain? Isme to Past Perfect nahi lagega? Ye to alag ho gaya!" },
        { "speaker": "aman", "text": "Bilkul sahi pakda — yahi exam ka twist hai. 'As soon as' khud hi 'turant baad' ka meaning deta hai, isliye dono actions Simple Past mein rehte hain, Past Perfect ki need nahi." },
        { "speaker": "raju", "text": "Toh 'As soon as he had seen me, he smiled' galat hoga!" }
      ],
      "navigation": { "next": "card_55_quiz1", "button_text": "Next Card ➔" }
    },

    {
      "card_id": "card_55_quiz1",
      "card_slug": "card_55_quiz1",
      "type": "quiz",
      "concept_id": "sequence_of_tense",
      "level": 7,
      "progress": { "current": 55, "total": 80 },
      "quiz_payload": {
        "question": "Sahi sentence chuno:",
        "options": [
          { "id": "A", "text": "No sooner he had reached office than it started raining." },
          { "id": "B", "text": "No sooner had he reached office than it started raining." },
          { "id": "C", "text": "No sooner had he reached office when it started raining." },
          { "id": "D", "text": "No sooner he reached office than it had started raining." }
        ],
        "correct_option_id": "B",
        "explanation": "'No sooner' ke baad Inversion hota hai (had+subject), aur connector 'than' aata hai, 'when' nahi. Dusra clause Simple Past mein hota hai."
      },
      "navigation": { "next": "card_56_quiz2", "button_text": "Check Answer & Continue ➔" }
    },

    {
      "card_id": "card_56_quiz2",
      "card_slug": "card_56_quiz2",
      "type": "quiz",
      "concept_id": "sequence_of_tense",
      "level": 7,
      "progress": { "current": 56, "total": 80 },
      "quiz_payload": {
        "question": "Error Detection: 'By the time the ambulance arrives (A)/ the patient had already (B)/ died due to excess bleeding (C)/ No error (D)'",
        "options": [
          { "id": "A", "text": "Part A" },
          { "id": "B", "text": "Part B" },
          { "id": "C", "text": "Part C" },
          { "id": "D", "text": "No error" }
        ],
        "correct_option_id": "A",
        "explanation": "'By the time' clause mein Simple Past aana chahiye jab main clause Past Perfect ho — 'arrives' galat, 'arrived' sahi hoga."
      },
      "navigation": { "next": "card_57_quiz3", "button_text": "Check Answer & Continue ➔" }
    },

    {
      "card_id": "card_57_quiz3",
      "card_slug": "card_57_quiz3",
      "type": "quiz",
      "concept_id": "sequence_of_tense",
      "level": 7,
      "progress": { "current": 57, "total": 80 },
      "quiz_payload": {
        "question": "'Hardly' aur 'Scarcely' ke saath kaunsa connector use hota hai?",
        "options": [
          { "id": "A", "text": "Than" },
          { "id": "B", "text": "When/Before" },
          { "id": "C", "text": "So that" },
          { "id": "D", "text": "As" }
        ],
        "correct_option_id": "B",
        "explanation": "'Hardly/Scarcely had...when/before' hota hai. 'Than' sirf 'No sooner' ke saath use hota hai — mixing karna common error hai."
      },
      "navigation": { "next": "card_58_milestone7", "button_text": "Check Answer & Continue ➔" }
    },

    {
      "card_id": "card_58_milestone7",
      "card_slug": "card_58_milestone7",
      "type": "milestone",
      "concept_id": "sequence_of_tense",
      "level": 7,
      "progress": { "current": 58, "total": 80 },
      "milestone_payload": {
        "title": "MODULE COMPLETED!",
