    },

    {
      "card_id": "card_67_error_detection_strategy",
      "card_slug": "card_67_error_detection_strategy",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "error_detection_master",
      "level": 9,
      "progress": { "current": 67, "total": 80 },
      "messages": [
        { "speaker": "aman", "text": "Ab hum wahi karenge jo SBI PO exam mein poocha jaata hai — sentence 4 parts mein todke error dhundhna. Strategy: 1) Pehle verb forms check karo (V1/V2/V3 sahi jagah?)." },
        { "speaker": "raju", "text": "Aur kya check karna hai sir?" },
        { "speaker": "aman", "text": "2) Time markers verb se match kar rahe hain kya (yesterday ke saath Simple Past hona chahiye, present perfect nahi)? 3) Subject-Verb agreement (was/were)? 4) Double past to nahi ho raha?" },
        { "speaker": "raju", "text": "Ye to ek checklist ban gayi sir! Chaliye practice karte hain!" }
      ],
      "navigation": { "next": "card_68_trap_irregular", "button_text": "Next Card ➔" }
    },

    {
      "card_id": "card_68_trap_irregular",
      "card_slug": "card_68_trap_irregular",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "error_detection_master",
      "level": 9,
      "progress": { "current": 68, "total": 80 },
      "messages": [
        { "speaker": "aman", "text": "Trap 1: Irregular Verb Wrong Forms. Exam mein invented wrong forms dete hain — 'catched' (sahi: caught), 'teached' (sahi: taught), 'writed' (sahi: wrote), 'seed' (sahi: saw)." },
        { "speaker": "raju", "text": "Sir ye sab to bilkul asli English words jaise lagte hain, dhoka ho jaata hai!" },
        { "speaker": "aman", "text": "Isiliye common irregular verbs V1-V2-V3 zaroor yaad karo: go-went-gone, do-did-done, see-saw-seen, write-wrote-written, take-took-taken, break-broke-broken." },
        { "speaker": "raju", "text": "Sir main roz 5 verbs yaad karunga, exam tak sab clear ho jaayenge!" }
      ],
      "navigation": { "next": "card_69_trap_double_past", "button_text": "Next Card ➔" }
    },

    {
      "card_id": "card_69_trap_double_past",
      "card_slug": "card_69_trap_double_past",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "error_detection_master",
      "level": 9,
      "progress": { "current": 69, "total": 80 },
      "messages": [
        { "speaker": "aman", "text": "Trap 2: Double Past Error — jab ek hi sentence mein do jagah past dikha diya jaaye. 'He did not went' (galat), 'He had went' (galat), 'I would have came' (galat)." },
        { "speaker": "raju", "text": "Toh sahi kya hoga in teeno ka sir?" },
        { "speaker": "aman", "text": "'He did not go', 'He had gone', 'I would have come'. Rule: 'did/had/would have' khud hi past/perfect dikha dete hain, isliye verb apni ORIGINAL form (V1 ya V3, situation ke hisaab se) mein rahegi." },
        { "speaker": "raju", "text": "Achhaaaa! 'Had' ke baad V3, 'did' ke baad V1, 'would have' ke baad V3 — teeno alag rule hain!" }
      ],
      "navigation": { "next": "card_70_trap_agreement", "button_text": "Next Card ➔" }
    },

    {
      "card_id": "card_70_trap_agreement",
      "card_slug": "card_70_trap_agreement",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "error_detection_master",
      "level": 9,
      "progress": { "current": 70, "total": 80 },
      "messages": [
        { "speaker": "aman", "text": "Trap 3: Subject-Verb agreement with was/were. 'Neither of the boys were present' — YE GALAT hai, kyunki 'Neither/Either/Each' singular maane jaate hain, 'was' aayega." },
        { "speaker": "raju", "text": "Hain?? 'Neither of the boys' to plural jaisa lagta hai sir!" },
        { "speaker": "aman", "text": "Yahi BPSC ka classic trap hai! 'Neither of', 'Either of', 'Each of' — sab SINGULAR treat hote hain. Sahi: 'Neither of the boys was present.'" },
        { "speaker": "raju", "text": "⭐ Note kar liya sir — 'of' ke pehle wala word dekho, boys nahi!" }
      ],
      "navigation": { "next": "card_71_trap_time_markers", "button_text": "Next Card ➔" }
    },

    {
      "card_id": "card_71_trap_time_markers",
      "card_slug": "card_71_trap_time_markers",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "error_detection_master",
      "level": 9,
      "progress": { "current": 71, "total": 80 },
      "messages": [
        { "speaker": "aman", "text": "Trap 4: Time Marker Mismatch. 'I have gone there yesterday' GALAT hai — 'yesterday' ek DEFINITE past time hai, isliye Present Perfect (have gone) nahi chalega, sirf Simple Past (went) chalega." },
        { "speaker": "raju", "text": "Toh Present Perfect ke saath 'yesterday, last year, ago, in 2015' jaise words kabhi nahi aa sakte?" },
        { "speaker": "aman", "text": "Bilkul sahi! Present Perfect ke saath 'already, just, yet, since, for, ever, never' aate hain — inko 'yesterday' jaise definite markers se kabhi mix mat karna." },
        { "speaker": "raju", "text": "Ye toh SBI PO ka sabse repeat hone wala trap lagta hai sir!" }
      ],
      "navigation": { "next": "card_72_quiz1", "button_text": "Next Card ➔" }
    },

    {
      "card_id": "card_72_quiz1",
      "card_slug": "card_72_quiz1",
      "type": "quiz",
      "concept_id": "error_detection_master",
      "level": 9,
      "progress": { "current": 72, "total": 80 },
      "quiz_payload": {
        "question": "Error Detection: 'The manager (A)/ has submitted the report (B)/ two days ago (C)/ No error (D)'",
        "options": [
          { "id": "A", "text": "Part A" },
          { "id": "B", "text": "Part B" },
          { "id": "C", "text": "Part C" },
          { "id": "D", "text": "No error" }
        ],
        "correct_option_id": "B",
        "explanation": "'Two days ago' ek definite past time marker hai, isliye Present Perfect (has submitted) nahi chalega. Sahi: 'submitted the report' (Simple Past)."
      },
      "navigation": { "next": "card_73_quiz2", "button_text": "Check Answer & Continue ➔" }
    },

    {
      "card_id": "card_73_quiz2",
      "card_slug": "card_73_quiz2",
      "type": "quiz",
      "concept_id": "error_detection_master",
      "level": 9,
      "progress": { "current": 73, "total": 80 },
